Prior art and references (informational; not bundled code)

The detection and normalization approaches implemented here draw on publicly
documented security research and standards. No third-party source code is
vendored from these projects:

  - NVIDIA garak, PR #1997 ("Turkish casefold buff"): the dotless-i casefold
    trap idea. https://github.com/NVIDIA/garak
  - Unicode Technical Standard #39, "Unicode Security Mechanisms" (confusables /
    restriction levels). https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr39/
  - Unicode Standard Annex #9, "Unicode Bidirectional Algorithm", and the
    "Trojan Source" research (CVE-2021-42574).
  - Unicode Technical Standard #55, "Unicode Source Code Handling".

The homoglyph mapping used here is a small curated subset inspired by the
UTS #39 confusables data, authored independently for this project.
